---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Pricing from '../components/Pricing.astro';
import Closing from '../components/Closing.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Faq from '../components/marketing/Faq.astro';
import '../styles/marketing.css';
const comparison=[
 ['Proposed price','$0 / trial','$29 / month','$99 / month','$299 / month','Custom'],
 ['Proposed credit allowance','1,000 trial','50,000 / month','250,000 / month','1,000,000 / month','Agreed with you'],
 ['Designed for','Evaluation','First integrations','Growing applications','Larger workloads','Custom requirements'],
 ['Source & route access','Approved profiles','Approved profiles','Approved profiles','Approved profiles','Scoped together'],
 ['Browser workflows','Separate qualification','Separate qualification','Separate qualification','Separate qualification','Scoped separately'],
 ['Actual project credits','Set by operator','Set by operator','Set by operator','Set by operator','Set by operator'],
 ['Account access','When configured','When configured','When configured','When configured','When configured'],
];
const faqs=[
 ['What is a credit?', 'Configured self-service credits are usage units for approved native HTTP operations. The operator sets route weights and credit policy; credits do not measure accepted records or provider invoices. Advertised commercial plan allowances and terms remain proposals.'],
 ['Are these plans available to buy now?', 'Prices and advertised allowances are commercial proposals. Plan buttons open signup with email verification when account access is configured. Your workspace shows the actual credit allocation set by the operator. Selecting a plan does not purchase or upgrade a plan, charge a payment method or start an automatic subscription. Paid access and commercial terms require approval.'],
 ['Does the free trial include every source and capability?', 'The 1,000 trial credits shown here are a proposed allowance. Actual trial eligibility and allocation come from the operator configuration and appear in your workspace. Self-service access supports approved native HTTP profiles and routes. Browser execution requires separate qualification.'],
 ['Are credits charged only when a request succeeds?', 'No. Admitted operations reserve configured credits. Dispatched work can consume credits even when the source returns a block or content your application cannot accept. Unknown outcomes retain their holds; confirmed cancellations before dispatch can release reservations. These credits are separate from provider invoices.'],
 ['What happens when I reach my allowance?', 'The service checks available project credits before admitting new work. Additional credits require operator approval. Selecting an advertised plan does not grant its proposed allowance, authorize overages or activate an automatic top-up.'],
 ['Do trial or monthly credits roll over?', 'Configured trial credits do not receive an automatic monthly refill. The monthly allowances shown here are commercial proposals; rollover, validity and renewal terms require a separate agreement.'],
 ['What if my project needs browser rendering or a specific country?', 'Share your target sources and required behavior during onboarding. We confirm approved proxy class and country combinations, browser recipe availability and the expected usage model before enabling the workload.'],
];
---
<Layout title="Pricing — FetchX" description="Compare proposed FetchX API prices and allowances. Actual project credits and native HTTP access depend on operator configuration; account signup does not purchase a plan." active="pricing">
 <div class="mkt"><div class="mkt-container"><header class="mkt-page-intro mkt-centered"><span class="mkt-eyebrow">A PLAN FOR YOUR NEXT BUILD</span><h1>Start exploring.<br/><span class="mkt-muted">Scale with a plan.</span></h1><p>From a first request to your next data product.<br/>Find a starting point for the way you build.</p></header><Pricing/>
 <section class="mkt-section" id="compare"><div class="mkt-section-heading"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">01 / THE PLANS, SIDE BY SIDE</span><h2>Find your<br/><span class="mkt-muted">starting point.</span></h2></div><p>Prices and allowances in this comparison are proposals. Actual credits and native HTTP access come from operator configuration; signup does not activate a commercial plan.</p></div><div class="mkt-comparison-wrap" tabindex="0" aria-label="Plan comparison. Scroll horizontally to compare all plans."><table class="mkt-comparison"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Plan details</th>{['Free','Developer','Growth','Scale','Enterprise'].map(name=><th scope="col">{name}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{comparison.map(([label,...values])=><tr><th scope="row">{label}</th>{values.map(value=><td>{value}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
 <section class="mkt-credit-section" id="credits"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">02 / UNDERSTAND THE UNIT</span><h2>A credit is a unit.<br/><span class="mkt-muted">Your workload gives it context.</span></h2><p>Different access routes and execution paths can involve different work. Confirm the credit model against your actual sources before planning a production budget.</p></div><div class="mkt-credit-factors"><article><Icon name="route" size={22}/><div><h3>Route & geography</h3><p>Direct, datacenter and other approved routes have different cost characteristics.</p></div></article><article><Icon name="code" size={22}/><div><h3>Execution path</h3><p>An HTTP fetch and a reviewed browser recipe can require different resources.</p></div></article><article><Icon name="layers" size={22}/><div><h3>Agreed project scope</h3><p>Capabilities, reservations and usage terms are confirmed for your project.</p></div></article></div></section>
 <section class="mkt-section mkt-faq-section"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">03 / THE COMMERCIAL DETAILS</span><h2>Before your<br/><span class="mkt-muted">first request.</span></h2><p class="mkt-faq-intro">Clear expectations for credits, capabilities and access.</p><a class="mkt-text-link" href="/contact">Discuss your workload <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></a></div><Faq items={faqs}/></section>
 </div><Closing/></div>
</Layout>
